{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793406754,"nonce":"HMQE+yuznI6H1uy03KHhkTifDZQ=","message":":checked/:disabled now work in the cascade: ElementState::is_pointer_driven excludes them from has_state(), so rules using them are base rules; they match the 'checked'/'disabled' attributes (class-list entries). Set by layout Button (disabled), Checkbox/Toggle (checked, disabled) and cn Switch (checked, disabled), Checkbox, Radio (checked); toggles in place via attr_when, tested. The older per-widget resolvers that read class_states for :checked/:disabled (toggle.rs, radio.rs, checkbox.rs, button.rs, text inputs) are unchanged and still run, so a rule can apply twice with the same values. Not yet emitting the attributes: layout Radio group, text inputs/areas (disabled), cn Toggle, ToggleGroup, input-otp, select/combobox triggers. Descendant rules like '.sw:checked \u003e .thumb' apply at build; after a toggle they wait for the next full style pass (class_when's documented limit).","files":null}]}